        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I noticed another case that triggered incorrect jumping: `:redrawstatus` called while in visual mode. Here are stack traces:\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<details>\r\n<summary style='cursor: pointer'><b>Stack traces</b></summary>\r\n\r\nHere it sets the later-incorrect position:\r\n\r\n```\r\n▸ ui_grid_cursor_goto(handle_T grid_handle, int new_row, int new_col) ui.c:473\r\n grid_puts_line_flush(_Bool set_cursor) grid.c:346\r\n grid_puts_len(ScreenGrid * grid, char * text, int textlen, int row, int col, int attr) grid.c:331\r\n grid_puts(ScreenGrid * grid, char * text, int row, int col, int attr) grid.c:153\r\n grid_putchar(ScreenGrid * grid, int c, int row, int col, int attr) grid.c:128\r\n draw_sep_connectors_win(win_T * wp) drawscreen.c:894\r\n win_update(win_T * wp, DecorProviders * providers) drawscreen.c:1911\r\n update_screen() drawscreen.c:581\r\n normal_redraw(NormalState * s) normal.c:1287\r\n normal_check(VimState * state) normal.c:1381\r\n state_enter(VimState * s) state.c:30\r\n normal_enter(_Bool cmdwin, _Bool noexmode) normal.c:471\r\n main(int argc, char ** argv) main.c:576\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere it sends the position:\r\n\r\n```\r\n ui_call_grid_cursor_goto(Integer grid, Integer row, Integer col) ui_events_call.generated.h:196\r\n ui_flush() ui.c:518\r\n inchar(char_u * buf, int maxlen, long wait_time) getchar.c:2834\r\n vgetorpeek(_Bool advance) getchar.c:2670\r\n vpeekc() getchar.c:1619\r\n char_avail() getchar.c:1643\r\n clear_showcmd() normal.c:2635\r\n showmode() screen.c:854\r\n▸ update_screen() drawscreen.c:612\r\n ex_redrawstatus(exarg_T * eap) ex_docmd.c:6137\r\n execute_cmd0(int * retv, exarg_T * eap, char ** errormsg, _Bool preview) ex_docmd.c:1621\r\n do_one_cmd(char ** cmdlinep, int flags, cstack_T * cstack, LineGetter fgetline, void * cookie) ex_docmd.c:2276\r\n do_cmdline(char * cmdline, LineGetter fgetline, void * cookie, int flags) ex_docmd.c:585\r\n do_cmdline_cmd(const char * cmd) ex_docmd.c:288\r\n nvim_command(String command, Error * err) vimscript.c:117\r\n nlua_api_nvim_command(lua_State * lstate) lua_api_c_bindings.generated.c:5515\r\n lj_BC_FUNCC :0\r\n lua_pcall(lua_State * L, int nargs, int nresults, int errfunc) lj_api.c:1116\r\n nlua_pcall(lua_State * lstate, int nargs, int nresults) executor.c:140\r\n nlua_schedule_event(void ** argv) executor.c:319\r\n state_handle_k_event() state.c:106\r\n nv_event(cmdarg_T * cap) normal.c:7386\r\n normal_execute(VimState * state, int key) normal.c:1172\r\n state_enter(VimState * s) state.c:88\r\n normal_enter(_Bool cmdwin, _Bool noexmode) normal.c:471\r\n main(int argc, char ** argv) main.c:576\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\nBut even after fixing that, there was some case in which the cursor was jumping. Patching all these places with additional `setcursor()` is probably wrong solution, so I found the place which calls `ui_call_grid_cursor_goto` inside `ui_flush` and added a check that ensures correct cursor position when nvim is in modes in which the cursor should be visible in editor window. I force-pushed the new solution, the old approach can be seen [in this diff](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/compare/cfdb4cbada8c65aa57e69776bcc0f7b8b298317a..e8bac63c4b75c56671c8ff47f57c1eaf6665a405).\r\n\r\nI am not sure if that's the best solution nor if I got all the modes correctly. I will be using nvim with this patch daily to test if there are any issues. If anyone would be willing to test this that would be helpful.",
