        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> From what I understand, Neovim does the redrawing by moving the cursor all around the screen and calling the drawing functions while the cursor is placed at drawing position.\r\n\r\n@jedrzejboczar This is not really true anymore. It used to work like this (with all the drawing code we inherited from vim), but drawing cursor and visible cursor are now separate. however, there are still quite some old code left around which conflates them. Instead of adding more `setcursor()` calls, which might cause other issues, I'd rather find all these invalid `ui_grid_cursor_goto()` calls and remove them (by invoking `grid_puts_line_flush(false)` explicitly), which we have gradually being doing over time.",
